-- title:
--   Smoothness of the integral model along the Gauss branch, q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$ and contains a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta)=\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L(\!(X)\!)$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField` of level $q^2M'$ and group $H=$ `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the unit reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$; thus $K$ is generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of that field of Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring, a domain with fraction field $L$, with perfect residue field, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A\to L$, and with maximal ideal generated by $\varpi$; let $A$ act on $K$ compatibly with $A\to L\to K$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent-series image the coefficientwise image `coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq` of the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant, and write $\mathfrak{X}=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and of $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ consisting exactly of those $f$ for which there are power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ not reducing to $0$ modulo the maximal ideal and $f\cdot y=x$ as Laurent series over $L$ (the Gauss valuation ring). Let $z\in\mathfrak{X}$ be a point at which the germ of the global section of $\mathfrak{X}$ obtained from $\varpi$ along `toBase` lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, so $z$ lies over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Assume: every point $y$ of either chart mapping to $z$ contains, in its prime ideal, every element of that chart algebra whose image in $K$ is a nonunit of $W_0$; and for every point $y$ of the finite chart mapping to $z$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ does not lie in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $\jmath\in\Omega$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\jmath$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Then there is an open subscheme $U\subseteq\mathfrak{X}$ containing $z$ such that the open immersion $U\to\mathfrak{X}$ followed by `toBase` is a smooth morphism.
--
--   This is the case $q=2$ of the smoothness statement for the two-chart normalisation over $A$ of the projective $j$-line in the function field of $X_H(q^2M')$: the model is smooth over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ near any point of the special fibre lying on the branch cut out by the Gauss valuation, provided the $j$-value there is not supersingular in the sense of `ssJSet`. It feeds the construction of the smooth Igusa base model through [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_opens_smooth_comp_toBase_of_goodPt_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_opens_smooth_comp_toBase_of_goodPt_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_two).
